"},{"id":"DeuteronomyBookof","title":"Deuteronomy, Book of"},{"id":"Hittites","title":"Hittites"},{"id":"JebusJebusite","title":"Jebus, Jebusite"},{"id":"JoshuaBookof","title":"Joshua, Book of"},{"id":"JudgesBookof","title":"Judges, Book of"},{"id":"LawBiblicalConceptof","title":"Law, Biblical Concept of"},{"id":"MarriageMarriageCustoms","title":"Marriage, Marriage Customs"},{"id":"Perizzite","title":"Perizzite"},{"id":"SamuelBooksofFirstandSecond","title":"Samuel, Books of First and Second"},{"id":"SlaveSlavery","title":"Slave, Slavery"},{"id":"WarHoly","title":"War*, Holy"},{"id":"Warfare","title":"Warfare"}],"dictionaryWords":[{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"When you go out to war against your enemies and see horses, chariots, and an army larger than yours, do not be afraid of them; for the LORD your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt, is with you.","verse":1},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"For the LORD your God goes with you to fight for you against your enemies, to give you the victory.”","verse":4},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"When the LORD your God has delivered it into your hand, you must put every male to the sword.","verse":13},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"But the women, children, livestock, and whatever else is in the city—all its spoil—you may take as plunder, and you shall use the spoil of your enemies that the LORD your God gives you.","verse":14},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"However, in the cities of the nations that the LORD your God is giving you as an inheritance, you must not leave alive anything that breathes.","verse":16},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"For you must devote them to complete destruction—the Hittites, Amorites, Canaanites, Perizzites, Hivites, and Jebusites—as the LORD your God has commanded you,","verse":17},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"so that they cannot teach you to do all the detestable things they do for their gods, and so cause you to sin against the LORD your God.","verse":18}],"id":"Lord","label":"LORD","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","scope":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","senseReview":"Only literal uppercase LORD is admitted globally. Source Lord article explicitly covers God as Lord; lowercase human lord and sentence-title Lord are not inferred from this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord","term":"LORD"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Lord","sourceTitle":"Lord"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Deut.20.4","r":"Deut.20.4","rawR":"Deut.20.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.20.4","value":"Deut.20.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"20:4"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["He will fight for you:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," This promise affirms that God initiates wars, carries them out, and brings them to successful conclusion against his enemies. The purpose of war initiated by God was to eradicate hopelessly unrepentant enemies and prevent them from contaminating his people (see ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.1.30","r":"Deut.1.30","rawR":"Deut.1.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.1.30","value":"Deut.1.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"1:30"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Deut.20.4","refs":[{"book":"DEU","endChapter":20,"endVerse":4,"startChapter":20,"startVerse":4}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Deut.20.4","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"DEU","sourceChapterCoverage":[20],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"30e925683b6e17c7f3d3aebdda63be8b0360186afc6b7220bf4ca4f9c7f88f23","sourceItemName":"Deut.20.4","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":2276,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"DEU","canonicalOSIS":"Deut","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Deut"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Deut.20.4","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Deut.20.4","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Deut.20.7","r":"Deut.20.7","rawR":"Deut.20.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.20.7","value":"Deut.20.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"20:7"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["someone else would marry her:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," In this situation, a man who died would be deprived of offspring to carry on his name, which was a great tragedy in ancient Israel."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Deut.20.7","refs":[{"book":"DEU","endChapter":20,"endVerse":7,"startChapter":20,"startVerse":7}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Deut.20.7","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"DEU","sourceChapterCoverage":[20],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"6eff774e6e4f8901a3a899294cc5c82f677889b59d3b2a9a26afc15c3a984683","sourceItemName":"Deut.20.7","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":2277,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"DEU","canonicalOSIS":"Deut","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Deut"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Deut.20.7","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Deut.20.7","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Deut.20.10-15","r":"Deut.20.10-15","rawR":"Deut.20.10-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.20.10-15","value":"Deut.20.10-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"20:10-15"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The people in the land had already been placed under the ban (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.7.1-6","r":"Deut.7.1-6","rawR":"Deut.7.1-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.7.1-6","value":"Deut.7.1-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:1-6"},"), so this instruction refers to those whom Israel would engage outside the land (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.20.15","r":"Deut.20.15","rawR":"Deut.20.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.20.15","value":"Deut.20.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"20:15"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Deut.20.10-15","refs":[{"book":"DEU","endChapter":20,"endVerse":15,"startChapter":20,"startVerse":10}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Deut.20.10-15","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"DEU","sourceChapterCoverage":[20],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"f007b317711b44435244c921d86e567c4f36a5675d1488d2a812f288bd0a