ring a war so the enemy could not benefit from them. However, since the Israelites were occupying the enemy’s former land, the trees could be of use to them."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Deut.20.19","refs":[{"book":"DEU","endChapter":20,"endVerse":19,"startChapter":20,"startVerse":19}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Deut.20.19","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"DEU","sourceChapterCoverage":[20],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"8e50d68e520670fbd5b94b694da7fbb27a77ac5d83a4ec2586e022ef8dbe19db","sourceItemName":"Deut.20.19","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":2281,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"DEU","canonicalOSIS":"Deut","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Deut"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Deut.20.19","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Deut.20.19","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Deut.20.20","r":"Deut.20.20","rawR":"Deut.20.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.20.20","value":"Deut.20.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"20:20"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," This ",{"c":["equipment"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," consisted of the materials built up against a city wall as part of the effort to bring it under siege."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Deut.20.20","refs":[{"book":"DEU","endChapter":20,"endVerse":20,"startChapter":20,"startVerse":20}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Deut.20.20","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"DEU","sourceChapterCoverage":[20],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b5ccf1a62ddc917ec61de19b7aea0ae35ebb0fcda0884ceedc99999df3f362db","sourceItemName":"Deut.20.20","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":2282,"sourceReferenceException":false,"source